i>\n\n\n\n<li>Understanding of data analysis concepts<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong design and analytical skills<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tools Used:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Power BI, Tableau, Microsoft Excel, SQL, and Python<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Average Salary:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>In India, Data Visualization Engineers earn an average of \u20b97,00,000 per year, while in the US, the average annual salary is approximately <a href=\"https:\/\/www.glassdoor.co.in\/Salaries\/united-states-data-visualization-engineer-salary-SRCH_IL.0,13_IN1_KO14,41.htm?countryRedirect=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">$106,000<\/a>, depending on experience, skills, and organization.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">10. Product Analyst<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>A Product Analyst analyzes product-related data to understand user behavior, improve product performance, and support product development teams in making data-driven decisions for better customer experience.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Job Responsibilities:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Analyzing product usage and customer behavior<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Monitoring product performance metrics<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Identifying product improvement opportunities<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Preparing product performance reports<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Supporting product strategy decisions<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Required Skills:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Knowledge of data analysis techniques<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Proficiency in Excel and SQL<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Understanding of product metrics<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Analytical and problem-solving skills<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tools Used:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Microsoft Excel, SQL, Google Analytics, Power BI, and Tableau<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Average Salary:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>In the US, Product Analysts earn an average salary of <a href=\"https:\/\/www.indeed.com\/career\/product-analyst\/salaries\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">$98,940<\/a> per year, while in India, the average annual salary is approximately <a href=\"https:\/\/in.indeed.com\/career\/product-analyst\/salaries\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">\u20b912,97,171<\/a>, based on experience, skills, and organization.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">11. Data Governance Analyst<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>A Data Governance Analyst ensures that organizational data is accurate, secure, and properly managed across departments. They develop and implement data policies, standards, and procedures that improve data quality, maintain compliance, and support reliable decision-making within the organization.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Job Responsibilities:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Creating and implementing data governance policies and standards<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Monitoring data quality, accuracy, and consistency<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Maintaining compliance with data privacy and security regulations<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Managing data classification and documentation<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Collaborating with IT and business teams to improve data management practices<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Required Skills:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Knowledge of data governance frameworks and policies<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Understanding of data privacy regulations<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Proficiency in SQL and data management tools<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tools Used:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Microsoft Excel, SQL, Data Governance Tools, Power BI, and Tableau<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Average Salary:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Data Governance Analysts in the US earn an average salary of <a href=\"https:\/\/www.indeed.com\/career\/data-governance-analyst\/salaries\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">$121,445<\/a> per year, while in India, the average annual salary is approximately <a href=\"https:\/\/in.indeed.com\/career\/data-governance-analyst\/salaries\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">\u20b98,05,605<\/a>, depending on experience, skills, and organization.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">12. Risk Analyst<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>A Risk Analyst evaluates potential financial, operational, and strategic risks that could impact an organization. They analyze data, assess uncertainties, and develop strategies to minimize losses while supporting informed and secure business decisions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Job Responsibilities:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Identifying and assessing financial and operational risks<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Analyzing data to evaluate potential threats<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Preparing risk assessment and compliance reports<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Developing risk mitigation strategies<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Monitoring regulatory and compliance requirements<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Required Skills:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Background in finance, economics, statistics, or business<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Strong analytical and critical-thinking skills<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Proficiency in Excel, SQL, and risk modeling techniques<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Knowledge of regulatory and compliance standards<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tools Used:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Microsoft Excel, SQL, Risk Management Software, SAS, and Power BI or Tableau<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Average Salary:<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Risk Analysts in the US earn an average salary of approximately <a href=\"https:\/\/www.indeed.com\/career\/risk-analyst\/salaries\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">$87,352<\/a> per year, while in India the average annual salary is around <a href=\"https:\/\/in.indeed.com\/career\/risk-analyst\/salaries\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">\u20b97,81,263<\/a> per year, depending on experience, skills, and organization.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-e709f5d66c078a6959413e097c45621b\"><strong>Read More Data Guides<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analyst-roadmap\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analyst Roadmap<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/future-of-data-analytics\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Future Scope of Data Analytics<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analytics-project-ideas\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">20+ Data Analytics Projects<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analyst-career-path\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Top Data Analyst Career Paths<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/programming-languages-for-data-analytics\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analytics Programming Languages<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-does-data-analyst-do\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">What Does a Data Analyst Do?<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Skills Required for a Career in Data Analytics<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>To build a successful data analytics career in 2026, you need a combination of technical knowledge, analytical thinking, and communication abilities to interpret data effectively and support decision-making. Below are the essential <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analyst-skills\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">skills required in data analytics<\/a>:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Data Analysis Skills:<\/strong> Strong data analysis skills help you examine large datasets, identify meaningful patterns, discover trends, and convert complex information into useful insights that support better business decisions and improve organizational performance.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Programming Knowledge:<\/strong> Proficiency in languages such as Python or R that help to you process data, run statistical analyses, automate tasks, and create effective data-driven solutions for business problems.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Statistical and Mathematical Knowledge: <\/strong>Understanding statistics, probability, algebra, and basic mathematical concepts helps you analyze data accurately, interpret results correctly, and apply appropriate analytical methods to solve real-world business problems.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Data Visualization Skills:<\/strong> These skills help you present data insights through charts, graphs, and interactive dashboards, making complex information clear and easy to understand for stakeholders, while supporting better communication, faster decision-making, and improved overall business performance.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Communication Skills:<\/strong> Strong communication skills allow you to clearly present your analytical findings, work effectively with different teams, and help organizations make well-informed decisions using data-driven insights.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Developing these essential skills can help you build a strong foundation and succeed in a data analytics career in today\u2019s data-driven business environment.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tools Used in Data Analytics Careers<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Below are the <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analytics-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">tools used in data analytics careers<\/a>:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Tool Name<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Purpose<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>Microsoft Excel<\/strong><\/td><td>Organizing data, performing calculations, creating reports, and building basic dashboards<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>SQL<\/strong><\/td><td>Extracting, querying, updating, and managing structured data from relational databases<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>Python<\/strong><\/td><td>Performing data analysis, automation, statistical modeling, and machine learning tasks<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>R<\/strong><\/td><td>Conducting statistical analysis, data modeling, and advanced data visualization<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>Power BI<\/strong><\/td><td>Creating interactive dashboards and business intelligence reports for decision-making<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>Tableau<\/strong><\/td><td>Designing visually engaging dashboards and presenting actionable insights<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>Google Analytics<\/strong><\/td><td>Tracking, measuring, and analyzing website and marketing performance data<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>Apache Spark<\/strong><\/td><td>Processing and analyzing large-scale datasets quickly using distributed computing<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>Hadoop<\/strong><\/td><td>Storing and managing massive volumes of structured and unstructured big data<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>SAS<\/strong><\/td><td>Performing advanced analytics, predictive modeling, and enterprise-level statistical analysis<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Career Growth Opportunities as a Data Analyst<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>A career in data analytics offers strong growth opportunities as you gain experience and expand your technical skills. You can start as a Data Analyst and gradually move into advanced roles such as Senior Analyst, Data Scientist, Data Engineer, or Analytics Manager based on your expertise and interests.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>With continuous learning in areas like machine learning, cloud computing, and business strategy, you can also transition into leadership roles such as Analytics Consultant or Chief Data Officer. The demand for data professionals continues to grow across industries, ensuring long-term career stability and competitive salaries.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-ccc32798605aa1e3b4a19d0b260b90ec\"><strong>Explore Our Data Related Courses<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/data-analytics-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Online Data Analytics Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Live Internship + 100% Job Support<\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/business-analytics-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Online Business Analytics Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Live Internship + 100% Job Support<\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/data-science-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Online Data Science Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Live Internship + 100% Job Support<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Industries Hiring Data Analytics Professionals<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Many industries are hiring data analytics professionals to analyze data, improve performance, understand customer behavior, and support better business decision-making processes. Below are the industries hiring data analytics professionals:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Healthcare Industry:<\/strong> Healthcare organizations use data analytics to improve patient care, monitor treatment outcomes, manage hospital operations, and support medical decision-making through accurate analysis of healthcare data.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Finance Industry:<\/strong> Financial institutions use data analytics to detect fraud, manage risks, analyze customer transactions, and improve investment decisions by identifying financial trends and patterns.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Retail Industry:<\/strong> Retail companies use data analytics to understand customer preferences, track sales performance, manage inventory, and improve marketing strategies for better customer engagement and sales growth.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Marketing Industry:<\/strong> Marketing companies use data analytics to measure campaign performance, study customer behavior, and optimize marketing strategies based on data-driven insights and trends.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Technology Industry:<\/strong> Technology companies rely on data analytics to improve product performance, monitor user behavior, enhance system efficiency, and support innovation through data-driven development strategies.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Working in these industries can provide you with diverse career opportunities and long-term growth in the field of data analytics.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read:<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analytics-course-syllabus\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analytics Course Syllabus<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to Start a Career in Data Analytics?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Starting a career in data analytics begins with building a strong foundation in statistics, mathematics and basic programming. You should learn tools like Excel, SQL, and Python to understand how data is collected, cleaned, and analyzed. Practicing with real-world datasets will help you strengthen your analytical thinking and problem-solving abilities.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Next, focus on gaining practical experience through hands-on projects. Create dashboards, analyze datasets, and build a strong portfolio that showcases your skills and understanding. You can also complete certifications and online training programs to enhance your knowledge and increase your job opportunities in the analytics field.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you want to become a Data Analytics professional, enrolling in a structured <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/data-analytics-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">data analytics course online<\/a> by <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">WsCube Tech<\/a> can help you learn step by step, gain practical exposure, and develop industry-ready skills more efficiently.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read:<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analyst-roadmap\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analyst Roadmap<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">FAQs About Data Analytics Careers<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block\"><div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831320023\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">1. What does a Data Analyst do?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">As a Data Analyst, you collect, organize, and study data to find useful patterns and trends. You use this information to help organizations understand performance, solve business problems, and make better decisions based on accurate insights from data analysis.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831326054\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">2. Is data analytics a good career option in 2026?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, a data analytics career in 2026 is a good option because many industries rely on data to improve performance and make decisions. You can find opportunities in finance, healthcare, retail, marketing, and technology sectors.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831339997\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">3. Do I need a degree to become a Data Analyst?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">You do not always need a degree to start a career as a data analyst. You can learn tools like Excel, SQL, and Power BI through online courses and develop practical skills by working on real-world projects.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831351286\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">4. What skills are required for a career in data analytics?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">To build a career in data analytics, you need skills such as data analysis, programming knowledge, statistics, data visualization, and communication. These skills help you understand datasets, interpret results, and support organizations in making better decisions.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831361638\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">5. Which programming languages are used in data analytics?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">In a <strong>data analytics career<\/strong>, you mainly use Python, R, and SQL. These languages help you clean data, perform statistical analysis, automate tasks, and manage databases efficiently in real-world projects.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831373212\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">6. How long does it take to become a Data Analyst?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">You can become a Data Analyst within three to six months by learning basic tools and concepts. With regular practice and project work, you can improve your skills and prepare yourself for entry-level data analyst careers.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831383702\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">7. How can freshers start a data analyst career?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">As a fresher, you can start a data analyst career by learning tools like Excel, SQL, and Python. Building small projects and gaining hands-on experience will help you understand real-world data problems and improve job opportunities.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831393539\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">8. What is the average salary of a Data Analyst?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">In a data analyst career, you can earn an average salary of around $84,000\u2013$90,000 per year in the US, while in India, you typically earn about \u20b96\u20138 LPA annually, depending on your experience, skills, and location.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831404851\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">9. Which industries hire data analytics professionals?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Many industries hire data analytics professionals, including healthcare, finance, retail, marketing, banking, and technology. You can work in different sectors based on your interests and apply your data analysis skills to solve business problems.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831415572\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">10. What is the difference between a Data Analyst and a Data Scientist?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">In data analysis careers, a Data Analyst focuses on analyzing data and creating reports, while a Data Scientist builds predictive models using advanced techniques. You work more on insights, whereas scientists handle machine learning and algorithms.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831427777\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">11. Is data analytics a stressful job?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">A career in data analytics is not always stressful, but you may face deadlines or complex datasets sometimes. With proper time management and practice, you can handle tasks easily and maintain a balanced work environment.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1771831438003\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">12. What is the future scope of data analytics?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">The future of data analytics is highly promising. As organizations increasingly rely on insights to enhance performance and make informed decisions, the demand for skilled professionals will continue to grow. You can expect expanding job opportunities, career advancement, and long-term stability across industries.<\/p> <\/div> <\/div>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/data-analytics-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogBanner&amp;utm_campaign=seo&amp;utm_page=\/data-analytics-careers\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\" noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1546\" height=\"381\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/09\/da-course-2.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-12831\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/09\/da-course-2.webp 1546w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/09\/da-course-2-300x74.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/09\/da-course-2-1024x252.webp 1024w, https: